[b]Overview[/b]

Community continuation of Neavo's Fast Insulated Self Sealing AirLock for current Oxygen Not Included builds.

[b]Features[/b]

[list]
[*]Adds a fast manual-style airlock.
[*]When set to Automatic or Locked, the door blocks gas, liquid, and heat transfer between its cells.
[*]Door opening speed is configurable. Default is 5x a native manual airlock.
[*]Debug Logging option writes detailed troubleshooting diagnostics to FISSAC.log next to Player.log.
[*]Bundled localizations: Czech, German, Spanish, French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, and Chinese.
[*]Supports Base Game and current gameplay DLC.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.4.1[/b]

[list]
[*]Restored the vanilla remote/tablet door work animation when ONI's static door override is initialized too early with a null animation entry.
[*]Kept the null override sanitizer in place so vanilla and modded doors still avoid AddAnimOverrides crashes.
[*]Confirmed by Workshop feedback that the animation fallback restores visible door-state work animations.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.4.0[/b]

[list]
[*]Added a Debug Logging mod option that writes detailed diagnostics to FISSAC.log next to Player.log.
[*]When enabled, logs mod lifecycle, Harmony patch installation, door prefab/spawn/state/cleanup events, and throttled cell samples around fast airlocks.
[*]Improved debug diagnostics: periodic leakage and insulation samples now run from the global sim tick, so FISSAC.log captures settled runtime door-cell state even when doors are idle.
[*]Removed misleading pre-spawn Door.IsOpen diagnostic noise from FISSAC.log.
[*]Cell samples include actual element, gas/liquid state, mass, temperature, insulation byte, liquid impermeability, and door/grid flags for the door cells and neighboring cells.
[*]Repaired zero fast-airlock PrimaryElement temperatures and delegated structure-temperature reads before vanilla door close sim messages to avoid Invalid cell modification warnings.
[*]Added bundled localization files matching the locale set currently shipped by Duplicant Status Bar.
[*]Added robust translation path resolution for locale aliases such as zh-CN, zh-Hans, and pt-BR.
[*]Added fallback loading for broken Workshop extraction paths that flatten translations files into the mod root.
[*]Refreshed translated building strings after translation load so the plan screen and building info use the selected language.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.3.5[/b]

[list]
[*]Split Harmony patch timing so database registration remains early, while Door and Workable patches are installed later in the mod load lifecycle. This reduces early vanilla Door initialization risk while preserving building registration timing.
[*]Kept the fast-airlock-specific worker animation lookup optional and non-logging.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.3.4[/b]

[list]
[*]Fixed a worker animation crash when duplicants change door control states. This could affect normal doors because ONI can initialize the shared door worker animation override before the animation asset is ready while this mod patches Door methods.
[*]The mod now sanitizes null door worker animation overrides after vanilla Door prefab initialization and before StandardWorker consumes door work animations, then keeps the fast-airlock-specific animation override scoped to this airlock prefab.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.3.2[/b]

[list]
[*]Scoped door Harmony patches to this airlock prefab so vanilla and other modded doors are not modified by the worker animation or cleanup patches.
[*]Re-applies sealed simulation state after vanilla door spawn and after vanilla SetSimState, reducing load-time and state-transition leak risk.
[*]Restores normal insulation when the door is explicitly set to Opened.
[*]Build/deploy cleanup now removes stale standalone PLib artifacts before copying the merged DLL.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.3.1[/b]

[list]
[*]Fixed completed-door spawn crashes in U59 by restoring the vanilla door rotation setting, which ensures ONI adds the Rotatable component that Door.OnSpawn now dereferences.
[/list]

[b]Version 0.3.0[/b]

[list]
[*]Rebuilt against the June 2026 ONI assemblies.
[*]Fixed the current [code]SimMessages.SetCellProperties[/code] and [code]ClearCellProperties[/code] API change that crashes old binaries.
[*]Uses a unique continuation static ID while preserving the saved-game building prefab ID.
[/list]

[b]Compatibility Notes[/b]

This continuation intentionally preserves the original saved-game building prefab ID:

[code]FastInsulatedSelfSealingAirLock[/code]

Existing doors from Neavo's original mod should resolve to this continuation in place. You should not need to deconstruct or replace them. ONI may still show a mod footprint mismatch warning because this continuation uses a different mod static ID, but the placed building ID is unchanged.

Disable the original workshop item before enabling this continuation. Both mods register the same building prefab ID, so running both together is not supported.

